  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-23T02:29:59.233Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the major point of pain with the 3.0 menu is that it totally locks out the ability to translate or rotate whilst the left or right menu is opened.\nA good way to mitigate this would be to create an option which requires the player to hold down a controller button to navigate the menu. When the button is not held down, the menu does not take away control.\nThe button would be best mapped to the side trigger/squeeze on Oculus Touch/Vive Wands, but would have to be B on Index controllers.\nAs an aside, this would allow for avatars with facial animations or other useful animations to keep the menu open, and rapidly change animations as needed.",
